---
import { agentClis, tools } from "../content/tools";
import Section from "./Section.astro";
---

<Section
	id="tools"
	eyebrow="What you need"
	title="It sits on top of the tools you already use"
	intro="Yellowhammer replaces none of them. You need a Mac on macOS 26 that stays awake through the Night, the Orca ADE, a Linear workspace, GitHub, and at least one supported agent CLI."
>
	<ul class="card-grid" data-cols="3">
		{
			tools.map((tool) => (
				<li class="card">
					<p class="card-tag">{tool.role}</p>
					<h3 class="card-title">{tool.name}</h3>
					<p class="card-body">{tool.body}</p>
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ul>

	<h3 class="subhead">Agent CLIs</h3>
	<p class="subhead-intro">
		The coding agents you already use in the terminal. They write the code. Each Work Card runs on a
		route: which agent CLI, model and effort level runs a piece of work.
	</p>
	<ul class="card-grid" data-cols="2">
		{
			agentClis.map((cli) => (
				<li class="card cli-card">
					<p class="cli-name">{cli.name}</p>{" "}
					<code class="cli-command">{cli.command}</code>
					<p class="card-body">Probed for unattended runs.</p>
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ul>
	<p class="fine-print">
		Adding another agent CLI takes an adapter and a probe, not a configuration edit.
	</p>
</Section>
